
there're two ways to copy branch commit to another
let's assume there're main and feature branch
you do some changes on main then create feature branch
git add commit them on feature branch, now main branch 
doesn't have those changes
one way is using 
git checkout main
git merge feature

another is using
git checkout main
git cherry-pick feature # this will copy feature's latest commit to main branch
or 
git cherry-pick commit-id # this will copy that commit id changes to main branch

git cherry-pick commit-id-A commit-id-B # copy two commit
git cherry-pick commit-id-A^..commit-id-B # copy from commit-id-A to commit-id-B, without ^ it will excluse A
